<article class="env-lemma" id="03SG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03SG">Lemma <span data-tag="03SG">59.83.7</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0A52" data-tag="0A52">59.83.1</a> assume $X$ is smooth. Let $j : U \to X$ an open immersion. Let $\ell $ be a prime number. Let $\mathcal{F} = j_!\underline{\mathbf{Z}/\ell \mathbf{Z}}$. Then statements (<a href="/tag/0A53" data-tag="0A53">1</a>) – (<a href="/tag/0A5A" data-tag="0A5A">8</a>) hold for $\mathcal{F}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since $X$ is smooth, it is a disjoint union of smooth curves and hence we may assume $X$ is a curve (i.e., irreducible). Then either $U = \emptyset $ and there is nothing to prove or $U \subset X$ is dense. In this case the lemma follows from Lemmas <a href="/tag/0A5B" data-tag="0A5B">59.83.2</a> and <a href="/tag/0GJA" data-tag="0GJA">59.83.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>